Sure, here's a simplified example of how you can use AJAX with PHP to dynamically populate the chat history inside the modal!

Let's assume you have already created a PHP file named `get_chat_history.php`, which queries and returns an array formatted like this:

```
[
   [
       "is_me" => true,
       "text" => "Hello! How can I assist you today?",
   ],
   [
       "is_me" => false,
       "text" => "Sure, what service are you looking for?",
   ],
  ...
]
```

Now let's modify the existing HTML template to bind event listener to an AJAX request:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>Chathistory Modal</title>

  <!-- Style sheets and jQuery library -->
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
  <script src="https://code.jquery.com/jquery-3.5.1.min.js"></script>

  <!-- Include your own scripts -->
  <script src="app.js"></script>
</head>
<body>

  <!-- Add a form element with input field for fetching data via POST -->
  <form method="post" action="get_chat_history.php">
    <input type="hidden" name="conversation_id" value="1234567890">
    <button type="submit" formTarget="modalContent" formMethod="GET">Show Chat History</button>
  </form>

  <!-- The modal and its contents -->
  <div id="chathistory-modal" class="modal">
      <div class="modal-content"></div>
  </div>

</body>
</html>
```

Next, add a container inside the modal to keep our chat history:

```html
<div id="modalContent" class="chat-history"></div>
```

Finally, modify your JavaScript to listen for form submit and render the chat history with the received data:

```js
// app.js

$(document).ready(function() {

  $("#chathistory-modal").on('shown.bs.modal', function() {
      $('#modalContent').empty(); // Clear out old content before appending new
      $('form').submit();
  });

  $('form').submit(function(e) {
    e.preventDefault();

    const conversationId = $(this).find('[name=conversation_id]').val();
    $.ajax({
        url: 'get_chat_history.php',
        dataType: "json",
        method: "POST",
        data: { conversationId },
        success: function(data) {
          // Loop over received data and append each message
          data.forEach((msg) => {
              const className = msg.is_me? "is-me" : "is-bot";
              const messageNode = $('<div/>', {'class': className})
                 .append($('<p/>').text(msg.text));

              $('#modalContent').append(messageNode);
          });
        }
    });
  });

});

$(window).on('load', function() {
  // Trigger modal show event after all content has been loaded, 
  // to ensure everything is ready for dynamic rendering
  $('#chathistory-modal').modal('show');
});
```

This implementation will send the specified `conversations_id` through POST request and pass back the JSON response to dynamically generate and append the related messages.

